# Rock 5B (RK3588) kernel patches

Buildroot applies every `*.patch` here to the kernel pinned by
`configs/rock5b_defconfig` (`BR2_LINUX_KERNEL_CUSTOM_VERSION_VALUE="6.18"`),
in lexical order: 0001 → 0002.

## 0001-rk3588-vendor-mpp-rga-drivers.patch  (~1 MB)
## 0002-rk3588-vendor-mpp-rga-dt.patch        (~15 KB)

The Rockchip vendor MPP codec (`rk_vcodec`: RKVENC2/VEPU580 encoder + RKVDEC2/
VDPU381 decoder + CCU) and RGA (`multi_rga`: RGA3 x2 + RGA2) drivers forward
ported to mainline 6.18, plus their RK3588 device-tree nodes and the Rock 5B
board `status = "okay"` enables.

Sourced verbatim from `yisding/rock-5b-ysp`:

    kernel-drivers/patches/rk3588-rkvenc2-01-vcodec-rga-drivers.patch
    kernel-drivers/patches/rk3588-rkvenc2-02-vcodec-rga-dt.patch

Both are generated against **pristine mainline v6.18** (`git am` anchor tip
`5614909e5803`), which is exactly why the kernel is pinned to `6.18` rather
than a later stable point release. The driver code is Rockchip vendor code
under GPL-2.0, forward-ported by ysp; see that repo's `LICENSE.md` for
provenance. They are vendored here as plain text (not Git LFS).

The matching `CONFIG_*` symbols are enabled in `../../kernel.config`
(`CONFIG_ROCKCHIP_MPP_SERVICE/RKVENC2/RKVDEC2/PROC_FS`,
`CONFIG_ROCKCHIP_MULTI_RGA/RGA_ASYNC/RGA_DEBUG_FS`). We use the **in-tree**
forward-port form (drivers built `=y`), matching ysp's "combined kernel". ysp's
DKMS out-of-tree variant is mutually exclusive with that (module exports clash
with vmlinux) and is **not** used here.

The userspace counterparts (`librockchip_mpp`, `librga`) and `ffmpeg-rockchip`
are separate Buildroot packages under `package/`.

## Fan note

No fan patch is needed. Mainline v6.18 `rk3588-rock-5b-5bp-5t.dtsi` already
defines `fan: pwm-fan` (pwm1 ch0, 50000 ns, `cooling-levels = <0 120 150 180
210 240 255>`, `fan-supply = <&vcc5v0_sys>`) and wires it into `package_thermal`
with active trips at 55 °C / 65 °C (1 s polling). `CONFIG_SENSORS_PWM_FAN` and
the thermal symbols in `../../kernel.config` make it functional. To retune the
curve on real hardware, add a small patch overriding `&package_thermal` trips.

## RKNPU note

The NPU driver is **not** forward-ported by ysp; it is built out-of-tree from
`package/rknpu` (lurenJBD `rk3588-rknn-core`, mainline binding). **No DT patch
is needed here.** Mainline v6.18 `rk3588-base.dtsi` already defines
`rknn_core_0/1/2` (`npu@fdab0000`/`fdac0000`/`fdad0000`,
`compatible = "rockchip,rk3588-rknn-core"`) plus `rknn_mmu_0/1/2`, and the Rock
5B board DT (`rk3588-rock-5b-5bp-5t.dtsi`) already flips all six to
`status = "okay"` with `npu-supply`/`sram-supply` wired to `vdd_npu_s0`. The
out-of-tree module's `of_match` (`rockchip,rk3588-rknn-core`) binds to those
enabled nodes when `rknpu.ko` loads. These nodes are also the binding of
mainline's own NPU driver Rocket (`CONFIG_DRM_ACCEL_ROCKET`, new in 6.18), so
`../../kernel.config` explicitly disables Rocket. Its kernel prerequisites are already set in
`../../kernel.config`: `MODULES`, `PM_DEVFREQ` + `DEVFREQ_GOV_SIMPLE_ONDEMAND`
(200-800 MHz DVFS), `IOMMU`/`ROCKCHIP_IOMMU` (per-core `rknn_mmu`),
`ARM_SCMI_PROTOCOL` (`SCMI_CLK_NPU`), and `DMA_CMA`/`DMABUF_HEAPS`.
